# Exercise 0 - Intro to Colab and Python Basics

The warm-up exercise for the course, mostly about getting comfortable with Colab and refreshing numpy, pandas, and seaborn before things get heavier.

## What I did

- Went through Colab basics and a few useful shortcuts (`Shift+Tab` for docs, `Ctrl+Space` for autocomplete)
- Numpy: reshaping vectors, creating arrays (`zeros`, `ones`, `eye`, `linspace`, etc.), indexing/masking, random numbers and basic stats
- Pandas: worked through the "10 minutes to pandas" guide, then used it on the California housing dataset. Checked for missing values, plotted income vs. house value, added a new feature (`rooms_per_person`)
- Seaborn: quick pairplot on the housing data, split by price category
- Trained a KNN classifier on MNIST digits, checked train vs. test accuracy, looked at which digits it got wrong, and tested how accuracy changes with different numbers of neighbors

## Takeaway

Less about results, more about getting the basic tools down before the real exercises start. The KNN part gave a first clear look at overfitting: training accuracy way higher than test accuracy as k gets smaller.
